var CONTENT={"1.1": {"h": "<h2>Internet, web and web technology<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The <b>Internet<\/b> is the global network of connected computers. The <b>World Wide Web<\/b> is one service on it: pages linked by hyperlinks, fetched with <b>HTTP/HTTPS<\/b>, addressed by <b>URLs<\/b>.<\/li>\n<li><b>How it works<\/b>: the browser (client) sends an HTTP <b>request<\/b> for a URL → DNS turns the domain into an IP address → the <b>web server<\/b> sends back a <b>response<\/b> (HTML, CSS, JS, images) → the browser renders it.<\/li>\n<li><b>Web technology<\/b> = the languages and tools for building this: HTML (structure), CSS (presentation), JavaScript (behaviour) on the <b>client side<\/b>; Node.js, Express and databases like MongoDB on the <b>server side<\/b>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Web page<\/th><th>Website<\/th><th>Web app<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>one HTML document<\/td><td>a collection of related pages under one domain<\/td><td>interactive software in the browser (Gmail, online banking)<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Static<\/b> sites send the same files to everyone; <b>dynamic<\/b> sites build pages per request from a database.<\/p>\n\n<h2>HTML document structure<\/h2>\n<p><b>HTML<\/b> (HyperText Markup Language) describes the <b>structure<\/b> of a page using <b>tags<\/b>. Current version: HTML5.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;My First Page&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h1&gt;Hello World!&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;This is a paragraph.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Part<\/th><th>Role<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>tells the browser this is HTML5<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;html&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>root element; <code>lang<\/code> gives the language<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;head&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>information about the page, not shown: title, meta, links to CSS, scripts<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;meta&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>metadata: charset, viewport (mobile), description, keywords<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;title&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>text on the browser tab<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;body&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>everything visible<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Syntax<\/b>: an <b>element<\/b> = start tag + content + end tag: <code>&lt;p&gt;text&lt;/p&gt;<\/code>. <b>Attributes<\/b> go in the start tag as name=\"value\": <code>&lt;img src=\"a.jpg\" alt=\"...\"&gt;<\/code>. <b>Empty<\/b> elements have no end tag: <code>&lt;br&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;hr&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;img&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;input&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;meta&gt;<\/code>. Comments: <code>&lt;!-- ... --&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Basic tags<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Tag<\/th><th>Use<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;h1&gt;<\/code> … <code>&lt;h6&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>headings, h1 largest<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;p&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>paragraph<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;br&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;hr&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>line break, horizontal rule<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;img src alt width height&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>image; alt is shown if it fails and read by screen readers<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;div&gt;<\/code> / <code>&lt;span&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>generic block / inline container, used for styling<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Text formatting<\/b>: <code>&lt;b&gt;<\/code> bold, <code>&lt;strong&gt;<\/code> important (bold), <code>&lt;i&gt;<\/code> italic, <code>&lt;em&gt;<\/code> emphasis, <code>&lt;u&gt;<\/code> underline, <code>&lt;mark&gt;<\/code> highlight, <code>&lt;small&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;del&gt;<\/code> struck out, <code>&lt;ins&gt;<\/code> inserted, <code>&lt;sup&gt;<\/code> superscript (A²), <code>&lt;sub&gt;<\/code> subscript (H₂O), <code>&lt;pre&gt;<\/code> keeps spacing, <code>&lt;code&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;blockquote&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Block vs inline elements<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Block<\/th><th>Inline<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>starts on a new line, takes full width<\/td><td>stays in the line, takes only its content's width<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>width/height/margins apply<\/td><td>width/height ignored<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>div, p, h1–h6, ul, ol, li, table, form, section<\/code><\/td><td><code>span, a, b, i, strong, img, input, label<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>CSS <code>display<\/code> can change either (see 1.6).<\/p>\n\n<h2>Semantic HTML5 elements<\/h2>\n<p>Tags that say what their content <b>is<\/b>: <code>&lt;header&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;nav&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;main&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;section&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;article&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;aside&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;footer&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;figure&gt;<\/code> + <code>&lt;figcaption&gt;<\/code>. They help search engines and screen readers, and make code readable, unlike a plain <code>&lt;div&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q1", "Nov25 Q2", "Nov25 Q11", "Nov24 Q1", "Nov24 Q7", "Nxt25 Q11", "RV1 Q9", "RPQ Q17"]}, "1.2": {"h": "<h2>Lists<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>List<\/th><th>Tags<\/th><th>Options<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Ordered (numbered)<\/td><td><code>&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;<\/code><\/td><td><code>type<\/code> = 1, A, a, I, i; <code>start=\"10\"<\/code>; <code>reversed<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Unordered (bullets)<\/td><td><code>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>CSS <code>list-style-type<\/code>: disc, circle, square, none<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Description / definition<\/td><td><code>&lt;dl&gt;&lt;dt&gt;term&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;meaning&lt;/dd&gt;<\/code><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Nesting<\/b>: put the inner list <b>inside<\/b> an <code>&lt;li&gt;<\/code>, before its <code>&lt;/li&gt;<\/code>. That is what the exam pictures (Coffee / Tea / Green tea) test.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;ol type=&quot;I&quot; start=&quot;10&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;Tea\n    &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Green tea&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Black tea&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n  &lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;Coffee&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;dl&gt;&lt;dt&gt;HTML&lt;/dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;structures a page&lt;/dd&gt;&lt;/dl&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<h2>Links<\/h2>\n<p><code>&lt;a href=\"URL\"&gt;text&lt;/a&gt;<\/code>. <code>target=\"_blank\"<\/code> opens a new tab.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Link<\/th><th>href<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>External site<\/td><td><code>https://www.karunya.edu<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Another page of the site<\/td><td><code>about.html<\/code> (relative path)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Bookmark on the same page<\/td><td><code>#contact<\/code>, pointing to <code>id=\"contact\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Email<\/td><td><code>mailto:admin@karunya.edu<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Phone<\/td><td><code>tel:+919876543210<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Image as a link<\/td><td><code>&lt;a href=\"...\"&gt;&lt;img src=\"...\"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n\n<h2>Images and media<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&lt;img src=\"pic.jpg\" alt=\"text\" width=\"300\"&gt;<\/code>; with a caption: <code>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;…&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><code>&lt;audio src=\"a.mp3\" controls&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;video src=\"v.mp4\" width=\"320\" controls autoplay muted loop&gt;<\/code>; several formats with <code>&lt;source src type&gt;<\/code> inside.<\/li>\n<li><code>&lt;iframe src=\"...\"&gt;<\/code> embeds another page: YouTube (<code>/embed/ID<\/code>), Google Maps.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h2>Tables<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Tag / attribute<\/th><th>Meaning<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;table&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;tr&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;th&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;td&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>table, row, header cell (bold, centred), data cell<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;caption&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>title above the table<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>&lt;thead&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;tbody&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;tfoot&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>group header, body and footer rows<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>colspan=\"n\"<\/code><\/td><td>cell spans n <b>columns<\/b> (merged across)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>rowspan=\"n\"<\/code><\/td><td>cell spans n <b>rows<\/b> (merged down)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>CSS <code>border<\/code>, <code>border-collapse: collapse<\/code>, <code>padding<\/code><\/td><td>borders, single lines, space in cells (older attributes: border, cellpadding, cellspacing)<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Method for \"draw this table\" questions<\/b>: count the real columns first. Write the rows top to bottom. A cell with <code>rowspan<\/code> takes up space in the rows below it, so those rows get <b>one fewer<\/b> <code>&lt;td&gt;<\/code>. Check that every row adds up to the same number of columns.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;table,th,td{border:1px solid #000;border-collapse:collapse;padding:4px 10px;text-align:center}&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;table&gt;\n  &lt;caption&gt;Seminar&lt;/caption&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th rowspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Day&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Sessions&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Morning&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Afternoon&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Mon&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;HTML&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;CSS&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Tue&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Project work&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q13", "Nov25 Q18a", "Nov25 Q19b", "Apr26 Q1", "Apr26 Q17a", "Apr26 Q17b", "May24 Q1", "May24 Q11", "May24 Q23b", "Nov24 Q23b", "Nxt25 Q1", "Nxt25 Q2", "Nxt25 Q17", "RV1 Q1", "RPQ Q16", "RPQ Q20", "RM1 Q5"]}, "1.3": {"h": "<h2>The form element<\/h2>\n<p><code>&lt;form action=\"/register\" method=\"post\"&gt;<\/code> collects input and sends it to the server.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Attribute<\/th><th>Meaning<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>action<\/code><\/td><td>URL that receives the data<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>method<\/code><\/td><td><b>GET<\/b>: data in the URL (<code>?name=ravi<\/code>), for searches; <b>POST<\/b>: data in the request body, for logins and registrations<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>target<\/code><\/td><td>_self (default), _blank (new tab)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>enctype=\"multipart/form-data\"<\/code><\/td><td>required for file uploads (with POST)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>autocomplete<\/code>, <code>novalidate<\/code><\/td><td>browser autofill on/off; switch off built-in validation<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n\n<h2>Input types and controls<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Need<\/th><th>Control<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Text, email, password<\/td><td><code>&lt;input type=\"text|email|password\"&gt;<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Number, range, date, time, color, tel, url, search<\/td><td><code>type=\"number\" min max step<\/code>, <code>type=\"date\"<\/code>, …<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>One of several<\/td><td><code>type=\"radio\"<\/code>, all with the <b>same name<\/b><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Several of several<\/td><td><code>type=\"checkbox\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Drop-down<\/td><td><code>&lt;select&gt;&lt;option&gt;<\/code> (<code>multiple<\/code> allows several; <code>&lt;optgroup&gt;<\/code> groups)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Multi-line text<\/td><td><code>&lt;textarea rows cols maxlength&gt;<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>File upload<\/td><td><code>type=\"file\" accept=\".pdf,.jpg\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Buttons<\/td><td><code>type=\"submit\"<\/code>, <code>type=\"reset\"<\/code>, <code>&lt;button&gt;<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Hidden value<\/td><td><code>type=\"hidden\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Suggestions<\/td><td><code>&lt;input list=\"x\"&gt;&lt;datalist id=\"x\"&gt;<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Labels and grouping<\/b>: <code>&lt;label for=\"id\"&gt;<\/code> ties text to a field (click focuses it; screen readers read it). <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;<\/code> + <code>&lt;legend&gt;<\/code> group related fields.<\/p>\n\n<h2>HTML5 validation attributes<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Attribute<\/th><th>Checks<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>required<\/code><\/td><td>field must not be empty<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>type=\"email\"<\/code>, <code>type=\"url\"<\/code><\/td><td>format<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>minlength<\/code>, <code>maxlength<\/code><\/td><td>text length<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>min<\/code>, <code>max<\/code>, <code>step<\/code><\/td><td>number/date range (age 18–25: <code>min=\"18\" max=\"25\"<\/code>)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>pattern=\"[0-9]{10}\"<\/code><\/td><td>regular expression (10-digit mobile); <code>title<\/code> gives the hint<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>placeholder<\/code><\/td><td>grey hint text (not validation)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>readonly<\/code>, <code>disabled<\/code>, <code>autofocus<\/code>, <code>checked<\/code>, <code>selected<\/code><\/td><td>state<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;form onsubmit=&quot;alert(&#x27;valid!&#x27;); return false;&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;fieldset&gt;&lt;legend&gt;Register&lt;/legend&gt;\n    &lt;label for=&quot;n&quot;&gt;Name&lt;/label&gt; &lt;input id=&quot;n&quot; name=&quot;name&quot; placeholder=&quot;Full name&quot; required&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;label for=&quot;e&quot;&gt;Email&lt;/label&gt; &lt;input id=&quot;e&quot; type=&quot;email&quot; name=&quot;email&quot; required&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;label for=&quot;m&quot;&gt;Mobile&lt;/label&gt; &lt;input id=&quot;m&quot; type=&quot;tel&quot; pattern=&quot;[0-9]{10}&quot; title=&quot;10 digits&quot; required&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    Mode: &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; name=&quot;mode&quot; value=&quot;Online&quot; required&gt; Online\n          &lt;input type=&quot;radio&quot; name=&quot;mode&quot; value=&quot;Offline&quot;&gt; Offline&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;select name=&quot;dept&quot; required&gt;&lt;option value=&quot;&quot;&gt;-- Dept --&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option&gt;CSE&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option&gt;ECE&lt;/option&gt;&lt;/select&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; required&gt; I agree&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt; &lt;button type=&quot;reset&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/fieldset&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>For the 12-mark form questions: use every control the question names, put a <code>&lt;label&gt;<\/code> on each, add <code>required<\/code> and the right types, and finish with a short table saying which tag does what.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q17", "Apr26 Q11", "May24 Q17", "Nov24 Q17", "Nxt25 Q16", "Nxt25 Q23", "RV1 Q2", "RM1 Q2", "RJS Q34", "RAS Q1"]}, "1.4": {"h": "<h2>CSS and how to add it<\/h2>\n<p><b>CSS<\/b> (Cascading Style Sheets) controls presentation: colours, fonts, spacing, layout. A rule = <b>selector<\/b> + <b>declaration block<\/b>: <code>h1 { color: maroon; font-size: 24px; }<\/code>. Each declaration is <code>property: value;<\/code>.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>How<\/th><th>Use<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Inline<\/td><td><code>&lt;p style=\"color:red\"&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>one element, quick tests<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Internal (embedded)<\/td><td><code>&lt;style&gt;…&lt;/style&gt;<\/code> in the head<\/td><td>one page<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>External<\/td><td><code>&lt;link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\"&gt;<\/code><\/td><td>whole site, one file to change<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Cascade<\/b>: when rules conflict, the more <b>specific<\/b> selector wins (inline &gt; id &gt; class/attribute/pseudo-class &gt; element); for equal specificity, the <b>later<\/b> rule wins; <code>!important<\/code> overrides both. Inline beats internal and external styles.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Selectors<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Selector<\/th><th>Example<\/th><th>Selects<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Universal<\/td><td><code>*<\/code><\/td><td>every element<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Element (type)<\/td><td><code>p<\/code><\/td><td>all &lt;p&gt;<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>ID<\/td><td><code>#menu<\/code><\/td><td>the element with id=\"menu\" (unique)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Class<\/td><td><code>.card<\/code><\/td><td>all elements with class=\"card\"<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Grouping<\/td><td><code>h1, h2<\/code><\/td><td>each listed<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Descendant<\/td><td><code>div p<\/code><\/td><td>p anywhere inside div<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Child<\/td><td><code>div &gt; p<\/code><\/td><td>p directly inside div<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Adjacent sibling<\/td><td><code>h2 + p<\/code><\/td><td>the p right after an h2<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>General sibling<\/td><td><code>h2 ~ p<\/code><\/td><td>every p after an h2 (same parent)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Attribute<\/td><td><code>input[type=\"text\"]<\/code><\/td><td>by attribute value<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Pseudo-class<\/td><td><code>a:hover<\/code>, <code>li:first-child<\/code>, <code>tr:nth-child(even)<\/code>, <code>input:focus<\/code><\/td><td>by state or position<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Pseudo-element<\/td><td><code>p::first-letter<\/code>, <code>p::first-line<\/code>, <code>::before<\/code>, <code>::after<\/code><\/td><td>part of an element<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Link states, in this order: <code>a:link<\/code>, <code>a:visited<\/code>, <code>a:hover<\/code>, <code>a:active<\/code>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  * { font-family: Arial; }\n  #title { color: crimson; }\n  .note { background: lightyellow; }\n  div &gt; p { border-left: 3px solid teal; padding-left: 6px; }\n  h3 + p { font-weight: bold; }\n  li:nth-child(even) { color: gray; }\n  p::first-letter { font-size: 1.4em; }\n  a:hover { color: red; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;h2 id=&quot;title&quot;&gt;ID selector&lt;/h2&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Heading&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Adjacent to h3, and has class note&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Direct child of div&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;one&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;two&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;three&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;four&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;hover me&lt;/a&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q12", "Apr26 Q2", "May24 Q12", "May24 Q18b", "Nov24 Q18b", "Nxt25 Q3", "Nxt25 Q6", "RV1 Q3", "RM1 Q3", "RPQ Q18"]}, "1.5": {"h": "<h2>The box model<\/h2>\n<p>Every element is a box: <b>content<\/b> → <b>padding<\/b> (inside the border, takes the background) → <b>border<\/b> → <b>margin<\/b> (outside, transparent).<\/p>\n<p><b>Total width<\/b> = width + padding-left + padding-right + border-left + border-right (margin is extra space around it). E.g. width 350, padding 15, border 4 → 350 + 30 + 8 = <b>388px<\/b>. With <code>box-sizing: border-box<\/code>, <code>width<\/code> already includes padding and border.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  .box { width: 200px; padding: 15px; border: 4px solid #c62828; margin: 20px; background: #fff8e1; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;content 200 + padding 30 + border 8 = 238px wide&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Shorthand order is <b>top right bottom left<\/b> (clockwise): <code>margin: 10px 20px 10px 20px<\/code>; two values = top/bottom, left/right. <code>margin: 0 auto<\/code> centres a block with a width.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Borders<\/h2>\n<p><code>border: 2px solid black<\/code> = width, style, colour. Styles: <code>dotted, dashed, solid, double, groove, ridge, inset, outset, none, hidden<\/code>; four values set each side: <code>border-style: dotted dashed solid double<\/code>. <code>border-radius<\/code> rounds corners (50% = circle).<\/p>\n\n<h2>Backgrounds and gradients<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>background-color<\/code>; <code>background-image: url(\"bg.jpg\")<\/code><\/li>\n<li><code>background-repeat<\/code>: repeat, repeat-x, repeat-y, no-repeat<\/li>\n<li><code>background-size<\/code>: cover (fill, may crop), contain (fit whole image), or px/%<\/li>\n<li><code>background-position<\/code>: center top, right bottom, …; <code>background-attachment: fixed<\/code> (stays when scrolling)<\/li>\n<li>Gradients: <code>linear-gradient(to right, red, yellow)<\/code>, <code>radial-gradient(circle, white, blue)<\/code>, <code>repeating-linear-gradient(...)<\/code><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h2>Colour, text and fonts<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Property<\/th><th>Example<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>color<\/td><td><code>red<\/code>, <code>#ff0000<\/code>, <code>rgb(255,0,0)<\/code>, <code>rgba(255,0,0,0.5)<\/code>, <code>hsl()<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>font-family, font-size, font-weight, font-style<\/td><td><code>Arial, sans-serif<\/code>; <code>16px / 1.2em / 120%<\/code>; <code>bold<\/code>; <code>italic<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>text-align, text-transform, text-decoration<\/td><td><code>center<\/code>; <code>uppercase<\/code>; <code>underline / line-through / none<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>line-height, letter-spacing, word-spacing, text-shadow, text-indent<\/td><td><code>1.5<\/code>; <code>2px<\/code>; <code>2px 2px 4px gray<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>opacity<\/td><td>0 (invisible) to 1 (solid); applies to the whole element<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>list-style-type<\/td><td>disc, circle, square, decimal, none<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Units: <b>px<\/b> fixed; <b>em<\/b> relative to the parent's font size; <b>rem<\/b> to the root's; <b>%<\/b> of the parent; <b>vw / vh<\/b> 1% of the viewport.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Transitions and animations<\/h2>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  .btn { background: #1565c0; color: #fff; padding: 10px 20px; border: none; transition: all 0.3s ease; }\n  .btn:hover { background: #ffb300; color: #000; font-size: 18px; }\n  .ball { width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; background: tomato; animation: move 2s linear infinite alternate; }\n  @keyframes move { from { transform: translateX(0); } to { transform: translateX(250px); } }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;button class=&quot;btn&quot;&gt;Hover me (transition)&lt;/button&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;ball&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><b>transition<\/b> animates a property change (e.g. on <code>:hover<\/code>) and reverses smoothly. <b>animation<\/b> + <b>@keyframes<\/b> runs on its own: name, duration, timing (linear/ease), iteration count (infinite), direction (alternate). <b>transform<\/b>: translate, rotate, scale.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q3", "Nov25 Q4", "Nov25 Q19a", "May24 Q2", "Nxt25 Q18", "RV1 Q10", "RV1 Q12", "RV1 Q13", "RM1 Q1", "RJS Q23", "Nxt25 Q21"]}, "1.6": {"h": "<h2>position<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Value<\/th><th>Offsets (top/left…) measured from<\/th><th>Keeps its space?<\/th><th>Typical use<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>static (default)<\/td><td>no effect<\/td><td>yes<\/td><td>normal flow<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>relative<\/td><td>its own normal place<\/td><td>yes<\/td><td>nudging; container for absolute children<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>absolute<\/td><td>nearest positioned ancestor (else the page)<\/td><td>no<\/td><td>badges, tooltips<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>fixed<\/td><td>the browser window; ignores scrolling<\/td><td>no<\/td><td>fixed headers, banners, help buttons<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>sticky<\/td><td>relative until the scroll offset is reached, then sticks<\/td><td>yes<\/td><td>sticky menus, table headers<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>z-index<\/b> sets the stacking order of positioned elements (higher = on top).<\/p>\n\n<h2>display, float and flexbox<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>display: block | inline | inline-block | none | flex | grid<\/code>. <code>none<\/code> removes the element (unlike <code>visibility: hidden<\/code>, which keeps its space).<\/li>\n<li><code>float: left | right<\/code>: pushes an element to one side and lets text wrap around it; <code>clear: both<\/code> stops the wrapping. This was the old way to make columns and nav bars.<\/li>\n<li><b>Flexbox<\/b> (one direction): <code>display: flex<\/code> on the parent; <code>flex-direction<\/code> (row/column), <code>justify-content<\/code> (main axis: flex-start, center, space-between, space-around), <code>align-items<\/code> (cross axis), <code>flex-wrap: wrap<\/code>, <code>gap<\/code>; children use <code>flex: 1<\/code> to share space.<\/li>\n<li><b>Grid<\/b> (two directions): <code>display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 10px;<\/code>; a child spans cells with <code>grid-column: span 2; grid-row: span 2<\/code>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h2>Navigation bar (a favourite 6-mark question)<\/h2>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  ul.nav { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #333; display: flex; }\n  ul.nav a { display: block; color: white; padding: 14px 24px; text-decoration: none; }\n  ul.nav a:hover, ul.nav a.active { background: #777; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;ul class=&quot;nav&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; class=&quot;active&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;News&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Steps: links in a <code>&lt;ul&gt;<\/code> → remove bullets and padding → put items side by side (<code>display: flex<\/code> on the ul, or <code>float: left<\/code> on the li) → make each link a block with padding and no underline → add <code>:hover<\/code> and an <code>.active<\/code> class.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Responsive design<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The viewport meta tag: <code>&lt;meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"&gt;<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><b>Media queries<\/b> apply rules only on some screens: <code>@media (max-width: 600px) { … }<\/code>. The widths where the layout changes are <b>breakpoints<\/b>. Also <code>@media (orientation: portrait|landscape)<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>Flexible sizes (%, fr, max-width: 100% on images) and flex/grid wrapping.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  .cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px; }\n  .cols div { background: #e3f2fd; padding: 10px; }\n  @media (max-width: 500px) { .cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;cols&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;Column 1&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Column 2&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Two columns, one column below 500px.&lt;/p&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q18b", "Apr26 Q18a", "Apr26 Q18b", "May24 Q18a", "Nov24 Q11", "Nov24 Q18a", "Nxt25 Q4", "Nxt25 Q5", "Nxt25 Q12", "Nxt25 Q13", "Nxt25 Q19", "RV1 Q4", "RPQ Q3", "RPQ Q19", "RM1 Q4"]}, "1.7": {"h": "<h2>What Bootstrap is<\/h2>\n<p><b>Bootstrap<\/b> is a free CSS (and JS) framework of ready-made classes for <b>responsive<\/b>, mobile-first pages: you add class names instead of writing CSS. Advantages: fast development, consistent look, responsive grid, works across browsers. Include it from a CDN:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css&quot;&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre>\n<h2>Containers and the grid<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>.container<\/code>: responsive fixed-width, centred box; <code>.container-fluid<\/code>: always full width.<\/li>\n<li>Grid: <code>.row<\/code> holds <code>.col-*<\/code> columns; each row has <b>12<\/b> units. <code>col-md-4<\/code> = 4/12 wide from the md breakpoint up (stacked on smaller screens). Breakpoints: sm 576, md 768, lg 992, xl 1200, xxl 1400 px. Plain <code>.col<\/code> = equal widths.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;container mt-3&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;col-sm-4 bg-primary text-white p-2&quot;&gt;col-sm-4&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;col-sm-8 bg-success text-white p-2&quot;&gt;col-sm-8&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-primary mt-3&quot;&gt;Primary&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-outline-danger mt-3&quot;&gt;Outline danger&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;alert alert-warning mt-3&quot;&gt;alert alert-warning&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<h2>Common classes<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Group<\/th><th>Classes<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Buttons<\/td><td><code>btn<\/code> + <code>btn-primary / secondary / success / danger / warning / info / light / dark / link<\/code>; <code>btn-outline-*<\/code>; sizes <code>btn-lg / btn-sm<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Colours<\/td><td>text <code>text-primary, text-danger…<\/code>; background <code>bg-success, bg-dark…<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Spacing<\/td><td><code>m-3, mt-2, mb-4, p-2, px-3, mx-auto<\/code> (m/p + side t b s e x y + size 0–5)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Text<\/td><td><code>text-center, text-end, fw-bold, text-uppercase<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Borders<\/td><td><code>border, border-primary, rounded, rounded-circle<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Alerts<\/td><td><code>alert alert-warning<\/code> etc.<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Tables<\/td><td><code>table table-striped table-bordered table-hover<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Images<\/td><td><code>img-fluid<\/code> (responsive), <code>rounded<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Forms<\/td><td><code>form-control, form-label, form-select, form-check<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Navbar<\/td><td><code>navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-dark bg-dark, navbar-brand, navbar-toggler, collapse navbar-collapse, navbar-nav, nav-item, nav-link<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Others<\/td><td><code>card, card-body, badge, dropdown, pagination, d-none / d-flex<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q7", "Apr26 Q12", "Nov24 Q8", "RV1 Q7", "RPQ Q7"]}, "2.1": {"h": "<h2>What JavaScript is<\/h2>\n<p><b>JavaScript<\/b> is the programming language of the web: it runs inside every browser (its <b>JavaScript engine<\/b>, e.g. V8 in Chrome) and makes pages interactive. It is interpreted/JIT-compiled, dynamically typed and event-driven, and with Node.js it also runs on servers. It is <b>not<\/b> related to Java apart from the name.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Where<\/th><th>How<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Internal<\/td><td><code>&lt;script&gt; … &lt;/script&gt;<\/code> in head or body (end of body is best, so the HTML exists first)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>External<\/td><td><code>&lt;script src=\"app.js\"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Inline event<\/td><td><code>&lt;button onclick=\"show()\"&gt;<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n\n<h2>Showing output<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>Where it appears<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>element.innerHTML = \"…\"<\/code><\/td><td>inside an HTML element (the usual way)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>document.write(\"…\")<\/code><\/td><td>into the page while loading (erases the page if called later)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>alert(\"…\")<\/code><\/td><td>pop-up box with OK<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>console.log(\"…\")<\/code><\/td><td>browser console (F12) / Node terminal<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>input.value = …<\/code><\/td><td>inside a text box<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Pop-up boxes<\/b>: <code>alert(msg)<\/code>; <code>confirm(msg)<\/code> returns true/false; <code>prompt(msg, default)<\/code> returns the typed text or null.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Variables and data types<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th><\/th><th>var<\/th><th>let<\/th><th>const<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Scope<\/td><td>function<\/td><td>block<\/td><td>block<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Re-declare<\/td><td>yes<\/td><td>no<\/td><td>no<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Re-assign<\/td><td>yes<\/td><td>yes<\/td><td>no<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Primitive types: <b>Number, String, Boolean, Undefined, Null, BigInt, Symbol<\/b>; reference type: <b>Object<\/b> (arrays and functions are objects). <code>typeof x<\/code> tells the type. Identifiers start with a letter, _ or $, and are case-sensitive.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Operators and conversions<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Arithmetic <code>+ - * / % **<\/code>; <code>++ --<\/code>; assignment <code>= += -=<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>Comparison: <code>==<\/code> compares after converting types (<code>\"5\" == 5<\/code> is true), <code>===<\/code> compares value <b>and<\/b> type (<code>\"5\" === 5<\/code> is false); <code>!= !== &gt; &lt; &gt;= &lt;=<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>Logical <code>&amp;&amp; || !<\/code>; ternary <code>cond ? a : b<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><code>+<\/code> with a string concatenates: <code>\"2\" + 3<\/code> = \"23\". Input box values are strings, so convert with <code>Number()<\/code>, <code>parseInt()<\/code> or <code>parseFloat()<\/code>. <b>NaN<\/b> = an invalid number; test with <code>isNaN()<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>Template literals: <code>`Hello ${name}`<\/code>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">let a = &quot;10&quot;, b = 5;\nconsole.log(a + b);            // &quot;105&quot;  (string)\nconsole.log(Number(a) + b);    // 15\nconsole.log(parseInt(&quot;42px&quot;)); // 42\nconsole.log(&quot;5&quot; == 5, &quot;5&quot; === 5, typeof null, typeof [], isNaN(&quot;abc&quot;));<\/pre>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q5", "Apr26 Q3", "Nov24 Q5", "May24 Q13", "Nxt25 Q7", "Nxt25 Q10", "RPQ Q1", "RPQ Q2", "RPQ Q12", "RJS Q1", "RJS Q2", "RJS Q5", "RJS Q6", "RJS Q9", "RJS Q18", "RJS Q19", "RJS Q39"]}, "2.2": {"h": "<h2>Control flow<\/h2>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">// if / else if / else\nif (marks &gt;= 90) grade = &quot;A&quot;;\nelse if (marks &gt;= 75) grade = &quot;B&quot;;\nelse grade = &quot;C&quot;;\n\n// switch\nswitch (op) {\n  case &quot;+&quot;: r = a + b; break;\n  case &quot;-&quot;: r = a - b; break;\n  default: r = &quot;invalid&quot;;\n}\n\n// loops\nfor (let i = 1; i &lt;= 5; i++) { }\nwhile (n &gt; 0) { n--; }\ndo { } while (false);\nfor (const x of [1, 2, 3]) { }      // values of an array\nfor (const k in obj) { }            // keys of an object<\/pre>\n<p><code>break<\/code> leaves a loop; <code>continue<\/code> skips to the next turn.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Functions<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Kind<\/th><th>Syntax<\/th><th>Notes<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Declaration<\/td><td><code>function add(a, b) { return a + b; }<\/code><\/td><td>hoisted: can be called before it is written<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Expression<\/td><td><code>const add = function (a, b) { return a + b; };<\/code><\/td><td>not hoisted<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Arrow<\/td><td><code>const add = (a, b) =&gt; a + b;<\/code><\/td><td>short; common as callbacks<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Parameters can have defaults (<code>function f(x = 1)<\/code>). A <b>callback<\/b> is a function passed to another function to call later (event handlers, <code>setTimeout<\/code>, <code>forEach<\/code>). Built-in functions: <code>parseInt, isNaN, alert, Math.max, Math.round, Math.random…<\/code><\/p>\n<p><b>Timers<\/b>: <code>setTimeout(fn, ms)<\/code> runs once after a delay; <code>setInterval(fn, ms)<\/code> repeats; stop with <code>clearTimeout / clearInterval<\/code>.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Arrays and objects<\/h2>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">let marks = [80, 92, 75];\nmarks.push(88); marks.pop(); marks.unshift(70); marks.shift();\nmarks.length; marks.indexOf(92); marks.includes(75);\nmarks.sort((a, b) =&gt; a - b); marks.reverse(); marks.join(&quot;, &quot;);\nmarks.slice(0, 2);                         // copy part\nmarks.map(m =&gt; m + 5);                     // new array, changed\nmarks.filter(m =&gt; m &gt;= 80);                // keep some\nmarks.reduce((sum, m) =&gt; sum + m, 0);      // one value: total\nmarks.forEach(m =&gt; console.log(m));\n\nlet s = { name: &quot;Ravi&quot;, dept: &quot;CSE&quot; };\ns.cgpa = 8.6; s[&quot;dept&quot;] = &quot;IT&quot;; delete s.cgpa;\nObject.keys(s); Object.values(s);<\/pre>\n<p>Strings have methods too: <code>length, toUpperCase(), toLowerCase(), trim(), split(\"\"), indexOf(), slice(), replace()<\/code>. Math: <code>Math.round, floor, ceil, pow, sqrt, max, min, random<\/code>.<\/p>\n\n<h2>The standard programs<\/h2>\n<p>All these are answered with a working page in the revision sets: palindrome, even/odd (<code>n % 2<\/code>), leap year (<code>(y%4==0 &amp;&amp; y%100!=0) || y%400==0<\/code>), largest, positive/negative/zero, prime (try divisors up to √n), factorial, Fibonacci, sum of an array, calculators, unit and currency converters, electricity bill slabs.<\/p>\n<p><b>Pattern for \"HTML page with embedded JavaScript\" questions<\/b>: inputs with ids → a button with <code>onclick=\"calc()\"<\/code> → in <code>calc()<\/code> read <code>.value<\/code>, convert with <code>parseFloat<\/code>, validate with <code>isNaN<\/code>, compute, write the result to an element's <code>innerHTML<\/code>.<\/p>\n\n<h2>Synchronous vs asynchronous<\/h2>\n<p><b>Synchronous<\/b> code runs line by line; each line waits for the previous one. <b>Asynchronous<\/b> code starts a slow job (timer, file, network, database) and continues; the result arrives later through a <b>callback<\/b>, a <b>Promise<\/b> (<code>.then()<\/code>) or <b>async/await<\/b>. This keeps pages and servers responsive.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">console.log(&quot;1&quot;);\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; console.log(&quot;3: after the delay&quot;), 0);\nconsole.log(&quot;2&quot;);\n// prints 1, 2, 3\n\nasync function load() {\n  const res = await fetch(&quot;https://api.example.com/data&quot;);   // waits without blocking the page\n  const data = await res.json();\n}<\/pre>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q14", "Nov25 Q20", "Apr26 Q19a", "May24 Q22", "Nov24 Q22", "Nxt25 Q9", "Nxt25 Q14", "Nxt25 Q15", "Nxt25 Q22", "RV1 Q11", "RPQ Q5", "RPQ Q9", "RJS Q3", "RJS Q8", "RJS Q11", "RJS Q13", "RJS Q14", "RJS Q15", "RJS Q16", "RJS Q20", "RJS Q22", "RJS Q25", "RJS Q26", "RJS Q28", "RJS Q29", "RJS Q30", "RJS Q32", "RJS Q35", "RJS Q41"]}, "2.3": {"h": "<h2>The DOM<\/h2>\n<p>The <b>Document Object Model<\/b> is the page as a tree of objects (nodes); <code>document<\/code> is the root. JavaScript changes the page by finding nodes and changing them.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Task<\/th><th>Methods / properties<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Find<\/td><td><code>getElementById, getElementsByClassName, getElementsByTagName, getElementsByName, querySelector, querySelectorAll<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Content<\/td><td><code>innerHTML<\/code> (with tags), <code>innerText / textContent<\/code> (text only), <code>value<\/code> (form fields)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Attributes and style<\/td><td><code>setAttribute, getAttribute, el.src, el.style.color, classList.add / remove / toggle<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Create / add / remove<\/td><td><code>createElement, createTextNode, appendChild, insertBefore, remove, removeChild<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Tables<\/td><td><code>table.insertRow(), row.insertCell(), table.rows, row.cells<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Navigate<\/td><td><code>parentElement, children, firstChild, nextElementSibling<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n\n<h2>Events<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Event<\/th><th>Fires when<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>click, dblclick<\/td><td>element clicked<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>mouseover, mouseout<\/td><td>pointer enters / leaves<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>keydown, keyup, input<\/td><td>typing<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>change<\/td><td>select/checkbox/input value changed<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>submit, reset<\/td><td>form submitted / reset<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>focus, blur<\/td><td>field gains / loses focus<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>load<\/td><td>page finished loading<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Attach a handler with an attribute (<code>onclick=\"f()\"<\/code>), a property (<code>el.onclick = f<\/code>) or <code>el.addEventListener(\"click\", f)<\/code> (several handlers allowed). The handler receives an <b>event object<\/b>: <code>e.target<\/code>, <code>e.key<\/code>, <code>e.preventDefault()<\/code> (stop a form submitting), <code>e.stopPropagation()<\/code> (stop bubbling up to parents).<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;input id=&quot;item&quot; placeholder=&quot;New task&quot;&gt; &lt;button id=&quot;add&quot;&gt;Add&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;ul id=&quot;list&quot;&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;p id=&quot;count&quot;&gt;0 tasks&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  document.getElementById(&quot;add&quot;).addEventListener(&quot;click&quot;, function () {\n    var text = document.getElementById(&quot;item&quot;).value.trim();\n    if (!text) return;\n    var li = document.createElement(&quot;li&quot;);\n    li.textContent = text + &quot; &quot;;\n    var del = document.createElement(&quot;button&quot;);\n    del.textContent = &quot;x&quot;;\n    del.onclick = function () { li.remove(); update(); };\n    li.appendChild(del);\n    document.getElementById(&quot;list&quot;).appendChild(li);\n    document.getElementById(&quot;item&quot;).value = &quot;&quot;;\n    update();\n  });\n  function update() {\n    document.getElementById(&quot;count&quot;).innerHTML = document.querySelectorAll(&quot;#list li&quot;).length + &quot; tasks&quot;;\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><b>Score-tracker pattern<\/b> (cricket, kabaddi, volleyball, basketball): keep the score in variables → each button calls a function that updates them → one <code>show()<\/code> function rewrites the scoreboard with <code>innerHTML<\/code>.<\/p>", "qs": ["Apr26 Q19b", "May24 Q3", "May24 Q19a", "Nov24 Q19a", "Nxt25 Q8", "Nxt25 Q24", "RAS Q2", "RJS Q4", "RJS Q7", "RJS Q10", "RJS Q17", "RJS Q21", "RJS Q36", "RJS Q37", "RJS Q38", "RJS Q40", "RJS Q42", "RJS Q43", "RJS Q44", "RJS Q45", "RJS Q46", "RJS Q47"]}, "2.4": {"h": "<h2>Why validate in the browser<\/h2>\n<p>Client-side validation gives instant feedback and stops obviously bad data before it is sent. It does <b>not<\/b> replace server-side checks (a user can bypass the browser).<\/p>\n<h2>Two layers<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li><b>HTML5 attributes<\/b>: <code>required, type=\"email\", minlength, min/max, pattern<\/code> (see 1.3).<\/li>\n<li><b>JavaScript<\/b>: <code>&lt;form onsubmit=\"return validate()\"&gt;<\/code>. The function checks each field and returns <code>false<\/code> to block submission, showing a message next to the field.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h2>Useful checks<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Rule<\/th><th>Check<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Not empty<\/td><td><code>v.trim() == \"\"<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Length<\/td><td><code>v.length &lt; 6<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Only letters<\/td><td><code>/^[A-Za-z]+$/.test(v)<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Letters and digits<\/td><td><code>/^[A-Za-z0-9]+$/<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Exactly 10 digits<\/td><td><code>/^[0-9]{10}$/<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Email<\/td><td><code>/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Has a digit<\/td><td><code>/[0-9]/.test(v)<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Number in range<\/td><td><code>!isNaN(v) &amp;&amp; v &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; v &lt;= 100<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Passwords match<\/td><td><code>p1 === p2<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Regex reminders: <code>^<\/code> start, <code>$<\/code> end, <code>[...]<\/code> one of, <code>{n}<\/code> exactly n times, <code>+<\/code> one or more, <code>\\d<\/code> a digit, <code>\\s<\/code> a space; <code>regex.test(string)<\/code> returns true or false.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;form onsubmit=&quot;return validate()&quot;&gt;\n  Name: &lt;input id=&quot;n&quot;&gt; &lt;span id=&quot;en&quot; style=&quot;color:red&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  Mobile: &lt;input id=&quot;m&quot;&gt; &lt;span id=&quot;em&quot; style=&quot;color:red&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n  &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;p id=&quot;ok&quot; style=&quot;color:green&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  function validate() {\n    var ok = true;\n    var n = document.getElementById(&quot;n&quot;).value.trim(), m = document.getElementById(&quot;m&quot;).value.trim();\n    document.getElementById(&quot;en&quot;).innerHTML = /^[A-Za-z ]{3,}$/.test(n) ? &quot;&quot; : (ok = false, &quot;Letters only, 3+&quot;);\n    document.getElementById(&quot;em&quot;).innerHTML = /^[0-9]{10}$/.test(m) ? &quot;&quot; : (ok = false, &quot;10 digits&quot;);\n    document.getElementById(&quot;ok&quot;).innerHTML = ok ? &quot;Valid&quot; : &quot;&quot;;\n    return false;   // demo: stay on the page\n  }\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q20", "RAS Q1", "RJS Q33", "May24 Q17"]}, "2.5": {"h": "<h2>JSON<\/h2>\n<p><b>JSON<\/b> (JavaScript Object Notation) is a lightweight, text-based format for storing and exchanging data, language-independent but based on JS object syntax. Used by APIs, config files and MongoDB.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Data in <b>name/value pairs<\/b>; keys must be in <b>double quotes<\/b>; objects in <code>{ }<\/code>, arrays in <code>[ ]<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>Value types: <b>string<\/b> (double quotes), <b>number<\/b>, <b>boolean<\/b>, <b>null<\/b>, <b>object<\/b>, <b>array<\/b>. No functions, dates, undefined or comments.<\/li>\n<li>Why JSON: smaller and easier to read than XML, parsed directly into objects.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">{\n  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Ravi&quot;,\n  &quot;age&quot;: 20,\n  &quot;active&quot;: true,\n  &quot;middleName&quot;: null,\n  &quot;address&quot;: { &quot;city&quot;: &quot;Coimbatore&quot;, &quot;pin&quot;: 641114 },\n  &quot;skills&quot;: [&quot;HTML&quot;, &quot;CSS&quot;, &quot;JS&quot;]\n}<\/pre>\n<h2>Converting<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Direction<\/th><th>Method<\/th><th>Name<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>object → JSON text<\/td><td><code>JSON.stringify(obj)<\/code><\/td><td>serialization (to store or send)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>JSON text → object<\/td><td><code>JSON.parse(text)<\/code><\/td><td>deserialization (to use the data)<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;table id=&quot;t&quot; border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Marks&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  var text = &#x27;[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Asha&quot;,&quot;marks&quot;:91},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;John&quot;,&quot;marks&quot;:78}]&#x27;;   // JSON text\n  var list = JSON.parse(text);                                            // -&gt; array of objects\n  list.forEach(function (s) {\n    document.getElementById(&quot;t&quot;).innerHTML += &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + s.name + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&quot; + s.marks + &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&quot;;\n  });\n  console.log(JSON.stringify(list[0]));   // back to text\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><b>JS object vs JSON<\/b>: an object literal is live code (keys may be unquoted, values may be functions); JSON is just a string in a strict format. Access parsed data with dot or bracket notation: <code>obj.address.city<\/code>, <code>obj.skills[1]<\/code>.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q22", "Apr26 Q5", "Apr26 Q14", "Apr26 Q21a", "May24 Q5", "May24 Q6", "May24 Q14", "May24 Q19b", "Nov24 Q3", "Nov24 Q13", "Nov24 Q19b", "RV1 Q6", "RPQ Q8", "RPQ Q11", "RPQ Q14"]}, "3.1": {"h": "<h2>What jQuery is<\/h2>\n<p><b>jQuery<\/b> is a small JavaScript <b>library<\/b> (\"write less, do more\"). It makes DOM selection, events, effects and AJAX shorter and handles browser differences. It is not a separate language: jQuery code is JavaScript.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;   &lt;!-- from a CDN --&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;js/jquery.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;                             &lt;!-- or a downloaded copy --&gt;<\/pre>\n<h2>Syntax<\/h2>\n<p><code>$(selector).action()<\/code>: <code>$<\/code> is the jQuery function; the selector uses CSS syntax; the action is a jQuery method. Methods can be <b>chained<\/b>: <code>$(\"#box\").css(\"color\",\"red\").slideUp().slideDown();<\/code><\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">$(document).ready(function () {      // run after the DOM has loaded\n  // all jQuery code here\n});\n$(function () { /* short form */ });<\/pre>\n<h2>Selectors<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Selector<\/th><th>Selects<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$(\"*\")<\/code><\/td><td>all elements<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$(\"p\")<\/code>, <code>$(\"#id\")<\/code>, <code>$(\".cls\")<\/code><\/td><td>by tag, id, class<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$(this)<\/code><\/td><td>the element the event happened on<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$(\"ul li\")<\/code>, <code>$(\"div &gt; p\")<\/code>, <code>$(\"h1, h2\")<\/code><\/td><td>descendant, child, group<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$(\"input[type='text']\")<\/code>, <code>$(\"[href]\")<\/code><\/td><td>attribute<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$(\"li:first\")<\/code>, <code>:last<\/code>, <code>:even<\/code>, <code>:odd<\/code>, <code>:eq(2)<\/code>, <code>:checked<\/code>, <code>:visible<\/code>, <code>:hidden<\/code><\/td><td>filters<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<h2>Events<\/h2>\n<p><code>click, dblclick, mouseenter, mouseleave, hover, keyup, keydown, change, submit, focus, blur<\/code>; general form <code>$(sel).on(\"click\", fn)<\/code>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;p class=&quot;t&quot;&gt;Click me&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;t&quot;&gt;Or me&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;input id=&quot;name&quot; placeholder=&quot;type&quot;&gt; &lt;span id=&quot;echo&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  $(function () {\n    $(&quot;.t&quot;).click(function () { $(this).css(&quot;color&quot;, &quot;crimson&quot;); });\n    $(&quot;#name&quot;).keyup(function () { $(&quot;#echo&quot;).text($(this).val()); });\n    $(&quot;p&quot;).on(&quot;dblclick&quot;, function () { $(this).hide(); });\n  });\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><b>jQuery vs JavaScript<\/b>: <code>$(\"#x\").hide()<\/code> vs <code>document.getElementById(\"x\").style.display = \"none\"<\/code>. jQuery is shorter and chainable and has effects built in; plain JS needs no extra download and is faster.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov24 Q2", "Nov24 Q12", "Apr26 Q4", "RPQ Q4", "RPQ Q6", "RPQ Q13"]}, "3.2": {"h": "<h2>Get and set content<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>Get<\/th><th>Set<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>text()<\/code><\/td><td>text content<\/td><td><code>.text(\"Hi\")<\/code> (tags shown as text)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>html()<\/code><\/td><td>content with tags<\/td><td><code>.html(\"&lt;b&gt;Hi&lt;/b&gt;\")<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>val()<\/code><\/td><td>a form field's value<\/td><td><code>.val(\"Ravi\")<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>attr()<\/code><\/td><td><code>.attr(\"href\")<\/code><\/td><td><code>.attr(\"href\", \"x.html\")<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>css()<\/code><\/td><td><code>.css(\"color\")<\/code><\/td><td><code>.css({\"color\":\"red\",\"font-size\":\"20px\"})<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Setters can take a callback: <code>$(\"p\").text(function (i, old) { return old + \"!\"; });<\/code><\/p>\n<h2>Adding and removing<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>Effect<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>append()<\/code> / <code>prepend()<\/code><\/td><td>insert at the end / start <b>inside<\/b> the element<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>after()<\/code> / <code>before()<\/code><\/td><td>insert after / before the element<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>remove()<\/code> / <code>empty()<\/code><\/td><td>delete the element / delete its children<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>addClass()<\/code>, <code>removeClass()<\/code>, <code>toggleClass()<\/code><\/td><td>change classes<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>width()<\/code>, <code>height()<\/code><\/td><td>dimensions<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<h2>Traversing<\/h2>\n<p>Up: <code>parent()<\/code>, <code>parents()<\/code>, <code>parentsUntil()<\/code>. Down: <code>children()<\/code>, <code>find()<\/code>. Sideways: <code>siblings()<\/code>, <code>next()<\/code>, <code>prev()<\/code>, <code>nextAll()<\/code>. Filtering: <code>first()<\/code>, <code>last()<\/code>, <code>eq(i)<\/code>, <code>filter()<\/code>, <code>not()<\/code>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;input id=&quot;v&quot; placeholder=&quot;item&quot;&gt; &lt;button id=&quot;add&quot;&gt;append&lt;/button&gt; &lt;button id=&quot;del&quot;&gt;remove last&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;ul id=&quot;l&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;first&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  $(function () {\n    $(&quot;#add&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#l&quot;).append(&quot;&lt;li&gt;&quot; + ($(&quot;#v&quot;).val() || &quot;new&quot;) + &quot;&lt;/li&gt;&quot;); $(&quot;#v&quot;).val(&quot;&quot;); });\n    $(&quot;#del&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#l li&quot;).last().remove(); });\n    $(&quot;#l&quot;).on(&quot;click&quot;, &quot;li&quot;, function () { $(this).toggleClass(&quot;done&quot;).css(&quot;text-decoration&quot;, $(this).hasClass(&quot;done&quot;) ? &quot;line-through&quot; : &quot;none&quot;); });\n  });\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><code>$(\"#l\").on(\"click\", \"li\", fn)<\/code> is <b>event delegation<\/b>: it also works for items added later.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q6", "Apr26 Q4", "Apr26 Q20a", "RV1 Q8", "RPQ Q13", "RPQ Q15"]}, "3.3": {"h": "<h2>Effects<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Group<\/th><th>Methods<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Hide / show<\/td><td><code>hide(), show(), toggle()<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Fade<\/td><td><code>fadeIn(), fadeOut(), fadeToggle(), fadeTo(speed, opacity)<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Slide<\/td><td><code>slideDown(), slideUp(), slideToggle()<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Animate<\/td><td><code>animate({css}, speed, callback)<\/code>: any numeric property (left, width, opacity, font-size…)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Control<\/td><td><code>stop()<\/code> ends the current animation; <code>stop(true)<\/code> also clears the queue; <code>delay(ms)<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Every effect takes an optional <b>speed<\/b> (\"slow\" = 600 ms, \"fast\" = 200 ms, or a number) and a <b>callback<\/b> that runs when it finishes. Effects on the same element run in a <b>queue<\/b>, one after another.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;a&quot;&gt;toggle&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;b&quot;&gt;fadeToggle&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;c&quot;&gt;slideToggle&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;d&quot;&gt;animate&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id=&quot;e&quot;&gt;stop&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;box&quot; style=&quot;width:120px;height:60px;background:teal;color:#fff;position:relative;margin-top:8px;padding:6px&quot;&gt;box&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  $(function () {\n    $(&quot;#a&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).toggle(&quot;slow&quot;); });\n    $(&quot;#b&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).fadeToggle(); });\n    $(&quot;#c&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).slideToggle(); });\n    $(&quot;#d&quot;).click(function () {\n      $(&quot;#box&quot;).animate({ left: &quot;220px&quot;, opacity: 0.5 }, 800)\n               .animate({ left: &quot;0px&quot;, opacity: 1 }, 800, function () { $(this).text(&quot;done&quot;); });\n    });\n    $(&quot;#e&quot;).click(function () { $(&quot;#box&quot;).stop(true); });\n  });\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p><b>Exam tip<\/b>: for \"show and hide product images / descriptions\" questions, start the elements with <code>display: none<\/code> in CSS, then give each button one effect inside <code>$(document).ready<\/code>.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q21", "Apr26 Q13", "Apr26 Q20b", "May24 Q4", "May24 Q23a", "Nov24 Q23a", "RV1 Q5", "RPQ Q10"]}, "4.1": {"h": "<h2>What React is<\/h2>\n<p><b>React<\/b> is a JavaScript <b>library for building user interfaces<\/b> from <b>components<\/b>, made by Meta. Key ideas:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Components<\/b>: reusable pieces of UI, written as functions that return what to show.<\/li>\n<li><b>JSX<\/b>: HTML-like syntax inside JavaScript.<\/li>\n<li><b>Virtual DOM<\/b>: React keeps a lightweight copy of the DOM, works out what changed, and updates only those parts of the real DOM, which is fast.<\/li>\n<li><b>One-way data flow<\/b>: data goes from parent to child through props.<\/li>\n<li><b>Single-page applications<\/b>: the page is built and updated by React instead of being reloaded.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Create a project: <code>npm create vite@latest myapp -- --template react<\/code>, then <code>npm install<\/code> and <code>npm run dev<\/code> (older: <code>npx create-react-app myapp<\/code>). The app starts at <code>main.jsx<\/code>, which renders <code>&lt;App /&gt;<\/code> into <code>&lt;div id=\"root\"&gt;<\/code>.<\/p>\n<h2>JSX rules<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Return <b>one<\/b> parent element (or a fragment <code>&lt;&gt;…&lt;/&gt;<\/code>).<\/li>\n<li><code>className<\/code> instead of <code>class<\/code>; <code>htmlFor<\/code> instead of <code>for<\/code>; every tag must be closed (<code>&lt;img /&gt;<\/code>, <code>&lt;br /&gt;<\/code>).<\/li>\n<li>JavaScript expressions go in braces: <code>{name}<\/code>, <code>{2 + 3}<\/code>, <code>{isLoggedIn ? \"Hi\" : \"Login\"}<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>Inline styles are objects: <code>style={{ color: \"red\", fontSize: \"20px\" }}<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>Component names start with a <b>capital letter<\/b>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h2>Components<\/h2>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div id=&quot;root&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/react@18.3.1/umd/react.development.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/react-dom@18.3.1/umd/react-dom.development.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/@babel/standalone@7.24.7/babel.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script type=&quot;text/babel&quot;&gt;\n  function Greet() {\n    return &lt;p&gt;Hi there!&lt;/p&gt;;\n  }\n\n  function Student(props) {                     // props = data from the parent\n    return &lt;li&gt;{props.name} - {props.dept}&lt;/li&gt;;\n  }\n\n  function App() {\n    const list = [{ id: 1, name: &quot;Asha&quot;, dept: &quot;CSE&quot; }, { id: 2, name: &quot;John&quot;, dept: &quot;ECE&quot; }];\n    return (\n      &lt;div&gt;\n        &lt;Greet /&gt;\n        &lt;ul&gt;\n          {list.map(s =&gt; &lt;Student key={s.id} name={s.name} dept={s.dept} /&gt;)}\n        &lt;/ul&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    );\n  }\n\n  ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById(&quot;root&quot;)).render(&lt;App /&gt;);\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Lists are rendered with <code>array.map()<\/code>; each item needs a unique <code>key<\/code>. (This preview loads React and Babel from a CDN so it runs in the browser; in a real project Vite compiles the JSX.) Older code uses <b>class components<\/b>: <code>class Greet extends React.Component { render() { return &lt;p&gt;Hi&lt;/p&gt;; } }<\/code>.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q8"]}, "4.2": {"h": "<h2>Props<\/h2>\n<p><b>Props<\/b> pass data <b>into<\/b> a component from its parent, like function arguments: <code>&lt;Student name=\"Asha\" /&gt;<\/code> → <code>props.name<\/code> (or destructured: <code>function Student({ name })<\/code>). Props are <b>read-only<\/b>.<\/p>\n<h2>State with useState<\/h2>\n<p><b>State<\/b> is data that belongs to a component and can change; changing it with the setter makes React re-render.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const [count, setCount] = useState(0);   // current value, setter, initial value\nsetCount(count + 1);                     // never change count directly<\/pre>\n<h2>Event handling<\/h2>\n<p>Events are camelCase and take a <b>function<\/b>, not a string: <code>onClick={handleClick}<\/code> or <code>onClick={() =&gt; setCount(count + 1)}<\/code>. Others: <code>onChange<\/code>, <code>onSubmit<\/code> (call <code>e.preventDefault()<\/code>), <code>onMouseOver<\/code>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div id=&quot;root&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/react@18.3.1/umd/react.development.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/react-dom@18.3.1/umd/react-dom.development.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/@babel/standalone@7.24.7/babel.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script type=&quot;text/babel&quot;&gt;\n  const { useState } = React;\n\n  function Counter({ step }) {\n    const [count, setCount] = useState(0);\n    return (\n      &lt;div&gt;\n        &lt;h3&gt;Count: {count}&lt;/h3&gt;\n        &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; setCount(count + step)}&gt;+{step}&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; setCount(0)}&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n        {count &gt;= 10 &amp;&amp; &lt;p style={{ color: &quot;green&quot; }}&gt;Reached 10!&lt;/p&gt;}\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    );\n  }\n\n  function Toggle() {\n    const [dark, setDark] = useState(false);\n    return (\n      &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; setDark(!dark)}\n              style={{ background: dark ? &quot;#222&quot; : &quot;#eee&quot;, color: dark ? &quot;#fff&quot; : &quot;#000&quot; }}&gt;\n        {dark ? &quot;Dark&quot; : &quot;Light&quot;} mode\n      &lt;/button&gt;\n    );\n  }\n\n  ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById(&quot;root&quot;)).render(&lt;div&gt;&lt;Counter step={2} /&gt;&lt;Toggle /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;);\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Props<\/th><th>State<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>passed in by the parent<\/td><td>owned by the component<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>read-only inside the component<\/td><td>changed with its setter<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>like function arguments<\/td><td>like the component's memory<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Conditional rendering<\/b>: <code>{cond ? &lt;A /&gt; : &lt;B /&gt;}<\/code> or <code>{cond &amp;&amp; &lt;A /&gt;}<\/code>. <b>useEffect<\/b> runs code after rendering (fetching data, timers): <code>useEffect(() =&gt; { … }, [deps])<\/code>.<\/p>", "qs": []}, "4.3": {"h": "<h2>Controlled form inputs<\/h2>\n<p>In React a form field's value is kept in <b>state<\/b>: <code>value={x}<\/code> plus <code>onChange={e =&gt; setX(e.target.value)}<\/code>. This is a <b>controlled component<\/b>: React always knows the current value.<\/p>\n<h2>Example: simple interest calculator (the class demo)<\/h2>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div id=&quot;root&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/react@18.3.1/umd/react.development.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/react-dom@18.3.1/umd/react-dom.development.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://unpkg.com/@babel/standalone@7.24.7/babel.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script type=&quot;text/babel&quot;&gt;\n  const { useState } = React;\n\n  function InterestCalculator() {\n    const [p, setP] = useState(&quot;&quot;);\n    const [r, setR] = useState(&quot;&quot;);\n    const [t, setT] = useState(&quot;&quot;);\n    const [si, setSi] = useState(null);\n\n    function handleSubmit(e) {\n      e.preventDefault();                       // stop the page reloading\n      if (!p || !r || !t) { setSi(&quot;Fill all fields&quot;); return; }\n      setSi((Number(p) * Number(r) * Number(t)) / 100);\n    }\n\n    return (\n      &lt;form onSubmit={handleSubmit}&gt;\n        &lt;h3&gt;Simple Interest&lt;/h3&gt;\n        Principal: &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; value={p} onChange={e =&gt; setP(e.target.value)} /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\n        Rate (%): &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; value={r} onChange={e =&gt; setR(e.target.value)} /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\n        Time (yrs): &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; value={t} onChange={e =&gt; setT(e.target.value)} /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\n        &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Calculate&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; onClick={() =&gt; { setP(&quot;&quot;); setR(&quot;&quot;); setT(&quot;&quot;); setSi(null); }}&gt;Clear&lt;/button&gt;\n        {si !== null &amp;&amp; &lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Simple Interest: {typeof si === &quot;number&quot; ? &quot;Rs. &quot; + si.toFixed(2) : si}&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;}\n      &lt;/form&gt;\n    );\n  }\n\n  ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById(&quot;root&quot;)).render(&lt;InterestCalculator /&gt;);\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>SI = P × R × T / 100. Each input is controlled by its own state; <code>onSubmit<\/code> calculates and stores the result in state, and the result line appears only once there is a value.<\/p>\n<h2>Structure of a small React app<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Split the page into components (Header, List, Item, Form), each in its own <code>.jsx<\/code> file with <code>export default<\/code> and <code>import<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li>Keep shared state in the nearest common parent and pass it down as props; pass <b>functions<\/b> down as props so children can update it (\"lifting state up\").<\/li>\n<li>Talk to a backend (Express) with <code>fetch<\/code> in <code>useEffect<\/code> or an event handler.<\/li>\n<\/ul>", "qs": []}, "4.4": {"h": "<p class=\"callout\">AngularJS is <b>not in 23CS2048<\/b>, which has React in its place. It is here only because the older 20CS2056 papers ask about it. Skip this page unless you are using those papers for practice.<\/p>\n<h2>AngularJS in one page<\/h2>\n<p><b>AngularJS<\/b> (1.x) is a structural JavaScript framework for single-page apps. It extends HTML with <b>directives<\/b> and keeps the view and data in sync with <b>two-way data binding<\/b>, following the MVC pattern.<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Directive<\/th><th>Role<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-app<\/code><\/td><td>root of the app<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-model<\/code><\/td><td>two-way binds an input to a variable<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-bind<\/code>, <code>{{ }}<\/code><\/td><td>show a value (one-way)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-init<\/code><\/td><td>initial values<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-controller<\/code><\/td><td>attach a controller ($scope)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-repeat<\/code><\/td><td>repeat an element per array item<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-click<\/code>, <code>ng-submit<\/code><\/td><td>events<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-show<\/code>, <code>ng-hide<\/code>, <code>ng-if<\/code>, <code>ng-disabled<\/code><\/td><td>conditional display<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>ng-view<\/code> + <code>ngRoute<\/code> / <code>$routeProvider<\/code><\/td><td>routing (single-page app)<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><b>Filters<\/b>: <code>{{ x | uppercase }}<\/code>, <code>lowercase<\/code>, <code>currency<\/code>, <code>date:'dd/MM/yyyy'<\/code>, <code>number:2<\/code>, <code>orderBy<\/code>, <code>filter<\/code>. <b>Form states<\/b>: <code>$pristine / $dirty<\/code>, <code>$valid / $invalid<\/code>, <code>$touched / $untouched<\/code>, <code>$error.required<\/code>, <code>$error.email<\/code>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"runbox\"><pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"html\">&lt;script src=&quot;https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/angularjs/1.8.2/angular.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;div ng-app=&quot;app&quot; ng-controller=&quot;c&quot;&gt;\n  Name: &lt;input ng-model=&quot;name&quot;&gt; &lt;p&gt;Hello {{ name | uppercase }}&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li ng-repeat=&quot;x in items&quot;&gt;{{ x }}&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;\n  &lt;button ng-click=&quot;items.push(&#x27;Item &#x27; + (items.length + 1))&quot;&gt;Add&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  angular.module(&quot;app&quot;, []).controller(&quot;c&quot;, function ($scope) {\n    $scope.name = &quot;ravi&quot;;\n    $scope.items = [&quot;Item 1&quot;];\n  });\n&lt;/script&gt;<\/pre><button data-run>See it run<\/button><\/div>\n<p>Every AngularJS question in the old papers is answered with a running example; use the links below.<\/p>", "qs": ["Apr26 Q6", "Apr26 Q7", "Apr26 Q15", "Apr26 Q21b", "Apr26 Q22a", "Apr26 Q22b", "May24 Q7", "May24 Q8", "May24 Q15", "May24 Q20a", "May24 Q20b", "Nov24 Q4", "Nov24 Q6", "Nov24 Q14", "Nov24 Q20a", "Nov24 Q20b"]}, "5.1": {"h": "<h2>What MongoDB is<\/h2>\n<p><b>MongoDB<\/b> is a <b>NoSQL document database<\/b>. Instead of tables with fixed columns it stores flexible, JSON-like <b>documents<\/b> (saved as <b>BSON<\/b>, binary JSON, which adds types like Date and ObjectId).<\/p>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>SQL<\/th><th>MongoDB<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>database<\/td><td>database<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>table<\/td><td><b>collection<\/b><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>row<\/td><td><b>document<\/b><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>column<\/td><td>field<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>primary key<\/td><td><code>_id<\/code> (added automatically as an ObjectId)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>fixed schema<\/td><td>schema-less: documents in one collection may differ<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>JOIN<\/td><td>embedded documents, or references by id (and <code>$lookup<\/code>)<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">{\n  _id: ObjectId(&quot;6b01fd2c5d1980c4c465b3b9&quot;),\n  name: &quot;Arun Kumar&quot;,\n  age: 45,\n  department: &quot;Cardiology&quot;,\n  address: { city: &quot;Coimbatore&quot;, pin: 641114 },   // embedded document\n  phones: [&quot;9876500001&quot;, &quot;9876500002&quot;]            // array\n}<\/pre>\n<p><b>Why use it<\/b>: flexible schema, data shaped like the JavaScript objects the app already uses, easy to scale horizontally (sharding), fast for reads and writes. The full name of a collection is the <b>namespace<\/b> <code>database.collection<\/code> (e.g. <code>hospitalDB.patients<\/code>).<\/p>\n<p><b>Tools<\/b>: the server <code>mongod<\/code>; the shell <b>mongosh<\/b> (<code>mongosh \"mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017\"<\/code>); the GUI <b>Compass<\/b>; Atlas (cloud).<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov24 Q10"]}, "5.2": {"h": "<h2>Databases and collections<\/h2>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">show dbs                        // list databases\nuse hospitalDB                  // switch to (and later create) a database\ndb.createCollection(&quot;patients&quot;) // create a collection (an insert also creates it)\nshow collections\ndb.patients.drop()              // delete a collection\ndb.dropDatabase()               // delete the current database<\/pre>\n<h2>CRUD<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Operation<\/th><th>Methods<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>C<\/b>reate<\/td><td><code>insertOne({...})<\/code> → insertedId; <code>insertMany([{...}, {...}])<\/code> → insertedIds<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>R<\/b>ead<\/td><td><code>find(filter, projection)<\/code> → all matches (a cursor); <code>findOne(filter)<\/code> → first match or null<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>U<\/b>pdate<\/td><td><code>updateOne(filter, {$set: {...}})<\/code>, <code>updateMany(...)<\/code>, <code>replaceOne(filter, doc)<\/code>; option <code>{upsert: true}<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><b>D<\/b>elete<\/td><td><code>deleteOne(filter)<\/code> → first match; <code>deleteMany(filter)<\/code>; <code>deleteMany({})<\/code> empties the collection<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">db.students.insertOne({ regno: 101, name: &quot;Asha&quot;, dept: &quot;CSE&quot;, cgpa: 8.9 })\ndb.students.insertMany([\n  { regno: 102, name: &quot;John&quot;, dept: &quot;ECE&quot;, cgpa: 7.6 },\n  { regno: 103, name: &quot;Divya&quot;, dept: &quot;CSE&quot;, cgpa: 9.2 }\n])\ndb.students.find()                                  // all\ndb.students.find({ dept: &quot;CSE&quot; })                   // filter\ndb.students.findOne({ regno: 102 })                 // one\ndb.students.updateOne({ regno: 102 }, { $set: { cgpa: 8.0 } })\ndb.students.updateMany({}, { $set: { year: 2 } })   // add a field to all\ndb.students.deleteOne({ regno: 103 })<\/pre>\n<p>Update operators: <code>$set<\/code> (set/add a field), <code>$unset<\/code> (remove), <code>$inc<\/code> (add a number: deposits and withdrawals), <code>$push<\/code> / <code>$pull<\/code> (array add/remove), <code>$rename<\/code>. An update result shows <code>matchedCount<\/code> and <code>modifiedCount<\/code>; a delete shows <code>deletedCount<\/code>.<\/p>\n<p>For the 12-mark \"illustrate the following operations\" questions: write one command per part, number them like the question, and show realistic sample data. The worked answers show real mongosh output.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q9", "Nov25 Q15", "Nov25 Q23", "Apr26 Q16", "Apr26 Q24", "May24 Q10", "May24 Q24", "Nov24 Q16", "Nov24 Q24"]}, "5.3": {"h": "<h2>Query operators<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Operator<\/th><th>Meaning<\/th><th>Example<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$eq, $ne<\/code><\/td><td>equal, not equal<\/td><td><code>{ status: { $ne: \"discharged\" } }<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$gt, $gte, $lt, $lte<\/code><\/td><td>&gt; ≥ &lt; ≤<\/td><td><code>{ experience: { $gt: 4.5 } }<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$in, $nin<\/code><\/td><td>in / not in a list<\/td><td><code>{ dept: { $in: [\"CSE\", \"IT\"] } }<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$and, $or, $not<\/code><\/td><td>logic<\/td><td><code>{ $or: [{ age: { $lt: 18 } }, { age: { $gt: 60 } }] }<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$exists<\/code><\/td><td>field present<\/td><td><code>{ email: { $exists: true } }<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>$regex<\/code><\/td><td>pattern<\/td><td><code>{ name: { $regex: \"^A\" } }<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Several fields in one filter are ANDed: <code>{ dept: \"CSE\", cgpa: { $gte: 8 } }<\/code>.<\/p>\n<h2>Shaping the result<\/h2>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"mongo\">db.students.find({}, { name: 1, cgpa: 1, _id: 0 })     // projection: only these fields\ndb.students.find().sort({ cgpa: -1 })                  // 1 ascending, -1 descending\ndb.students.find().sort({ cgpa: -1 }).limit(3)         // top 3\ndb.students.find().skip(10).limit(10)                  // page 2\ndb.students.countDocuments({ dept: &quot;CSE&quot; })            // count\ndb.students.distinct(&quot;dept&quot;)                           // unique values\ndb.students.aggregate([{ $group: { _id: &quot;$dept&quot;, avg: { $avg: &quot;$cgpa&quot; } } }])   // group and average<\/pre>\n<p>Indexes speed up searches on a field: <code>db.students.createIndex({ regno: 1 }, { unique: true })<\/code> also stops duplicate register numbers.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q23", "Apr26 Q24", "May24 Q24", "Nov24 Q24"]}, "5.4": {"h": "<h2>Mongoose<\/h2>\n<p><b>Mongoose<\/b> is an <b>ODM<\/b> (Object Data Modeling) library for using MongoDB from Node.js. It adds a <b>schema<\/b> (field types, required, defaults, validation) on top of schema-less MongoDB, and gives a <b>model<\/b> with simple async methods. Install with <code>npm install mongoose<\/code>.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const mongoose = require(&quot;mongoose&quot;);\n\n// 1. connect\nmongoose.connect(&quot;mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/collegeDB&quot;)\n  .then(() =&gt; console.log(&quot;Connected&quot;))\n  .catch(err =&gt; console.log(err.message));\n\n// 2. schema: shape and rules\nconst studentSchema = new mongoose.Schema({\n  name:  { type: String, required: true, unique: true },\n  dept:  { type: String, enum: [&quot;CSE&quot;, &quot;ECE&quot;, &quot;IT&quot;] },\n  cgpa:  { type: Number, min: 0, max: 10 },\n  joined: { type: Date, default: Date.now }\n});\n\n// 3. model: the collection (&quot;students&quot;)\nconst Student = mongoose.model(&quot;Student&quot;, studentSchema);\n\n// 4. CRUD (inside an async function)\nawait Student.create({ name: &quot;Asha&quot;, dept: &quot;CSE&quot;, cgpa: 8.9 });     // or new Student({...}).save()\nconst all = await Student.find({ dept: &quot;CSE&quot; });\nconst one = await Student.findOne({ name: &quot;Asha&quot; });\nawait Student.updateOne({ name: &quot;Asha&quot; }, { cgpa: 9.1 });\nawait Student.findOneAndUpdate({ name: &quot;Asha&quot; }, { cgpa: 9.2 }, { new: true });   // returns the updated doc\nawait Student.deleteOne({ name: &quot;Asha&quot; });<\/pre>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Error<\/th><th>When<\/th><th>Send<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>err.name === \"ValidationError\"<\/code><\/td><td>a schema rule fails (required, min/max, enum)<\/td><td>400<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td><code>err.code === 11000<\/code><\/td><td>a <code>unique<\/code> field is duplicated<\/td><td>409<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>other<\/td><td>database down, bad id<\/td><td>500<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><code>{ new: true }<\/code> makes <code>findOneAndUpdate<\/code> return the updated document; the newest Mongoose versions prefer <code>{ returnDocument: \"after\" }<\/code> and print a deprecation warning for <code>new<\/code>, but both work.<\/p>\n<p>The model name \"Student\" becomes the collection <code>students<\/code> (lower-case plural) unless a third argument names it.<\/p>", "qs": ["Apr26 Q10", "Nov25 Q24", "Apr26 Q23", "RAS Q3"]}, "6.1": {"h": "<h2>What Node.js is<\/h2>\n<p><b>Node.js<\/b> is a <b>runtime environment<\/b> that runs JavaScript <b>outside the browser<\/b>, on the server, using Chrome's V8 engine. It is used for web servers, APIs, command-line tools and real-time apps (chat).<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Single-threaded, event-driven, non-blocking I/O<\/b>: slow work (files, network, database) is handed off, and Node keeps serving other requests; when the work finishes, its callback is queued.<\/li>\n<li>Same language on the front end and back end; a huge package ecosystem (<b>npm<\/b>).<\/li>\n<li>No DOM or <code>window<\/code>; instead <code>require<\/code>, <code>process<\/code>, <code>__dirname<\/code> and built-in modules.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h2>The event loop<\/h2>\n<p>Node runs your code once, top to bottom. Asynchronous calls (<code>setTimeout<\/code>, <code>fs.readFile<\/code>, database queries, incoming requests) register a callback and return immediately. The <b>event loop<\/b> keeps checking the queue and runs each callback when its work is done. This is why one thread can serve thousands of connections.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">console.log(&quot;This is the first statement&quot;);\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; console.log(&quot;This is the timeout callback&quot;), 0);\nconsole.log(&quot;This is the second statement&quot;);\n// first, second, then the timeout callback (it waits for the call stack to empty)<\/pre>\n<p><b>Synchronous vs asynchronous<\/b>: <code>fs.readFileSync()<\/code> blocks until done; <code>fs.readFile(…, callback)<\/code> does not. Prefer async on servers. Modern style: Promises with <code>async/await<\/code> (<code>await fs.promises.readFile(...)<\/code>).<\/p>\n<h2>Modules and npm<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Kind<\/th><th>Example<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Built-in (core)<\/td><td><code>http, fs, path, os, url, events, querystring<\/code>: <code>const fs = require(\"fs\");<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Your own (user-defined)<\/td><td><code>module.exports = { add };<\/code> in math.js → <code>const { add } = require(\"./math\");<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Third-party (npm)<\/td><td><code>npm install express<\/code> → <code>require(\"express\")<\/code>; listed in package.json; files in node_modules<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p><code>npm init -y<\/code> creates package.json. ES-module syntax (<code>import<\/code> / <code>export<\/code>) also works with <code>\"type\": \"module\"<\/code>.<\/p>\n<p><b>Events module<\/b>: <code>const EventEmitter = require(\"events\"); const e = new EventEmitter(); e.on(\"greet\", n =&gt; console.log(\"Hi \" + n)); e.emit(\"greet\", \"Ravi\");<\/code>. This is event-driven programming in miniature.<\/p>", "qs": ["Apr26 Q9", "May24 Q9", "Nxt25 Q9", "RJS Q16"]}, "6.2": {"h": "<h2>The http module: a web server<\/h2>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const http = require(&quot;http&quot;);\n\nhttp.createServer((req, res) =&gt; {          // runs for every request\n  if (req.url === &quot;/&quot;) {\n    res.writeHead(200, { &quot;Content-Type&quot;: &quot;text/html&quot; });\n    res.end(&quot;&lt;h1&gt;Home&lt;/h1&gt;&quot;);\n  } else {\n    res.writeHead(404, { &quot;Content-Type&quot;: &quot;text/plain&quot; });\n    res.end(&quot;Not found&quot;);\n  }\n}).listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;http://localhost:3000&quot;));<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li><code>req<\/code>: the request: <code>req.url<\/code>, <code>req.method<\/code>, <code>req.headers<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><code>res<\/code>: the response: <code>writeHead(status, headers)<\/code>, <code>write()<\/code>, <code>end()<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><b>Reading a POSTed form<\/b> without Express: the body arrives in chunks: <code>req.on(\"data\", c =&gt; body += c)<\/code>, then <code>req.on(\"end\", …)<\/code> and <code>querystring.parse(body)<\/code>. To serve an HTML file, <code>fs.readFile(\"form.html\", …)<\/code> and send it.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h2>The fs module: files<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Task<\/th><th>Async (callback)<\/th><th>Sync<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Read<\/td><td><code>fs.readFile(\"a.txt\", \"utf8\", (err, data) =&gt; …)<\/code><\/td><td><code>fs.readFileSync(\"a.txt\", \"utf8\")<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Write (replace)<\/td><td><code>fs.writeFile(\"a.txt\", \"Hello\", err =&gt; …)<\/code><\/td><td><code>fs.writeFileSync<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Append<\/td><td><code>fs.appendFile(\"a.txt\", \"more\\n\", err =&gt; …)<\/code><\/td><td><code>fs.appendFileSync<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Delete / rename<\/td><td><code>fs.unlink<\/code>, <code>fs.rename<\/code><\/td><td><code>fs.unlinkSync<\/code>…<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Exists / folder<\/td><td><\/td><td><code>fs.existsSync<\/code>, <code>fs.mkdirSync<\/code><\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Callbacks receive the error first (<code>err<\/code>), the Node convention; always check it.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q16", "Apr26 Q8", "Nov24 Q9", "Nov24 Q15", "May24 Q16", "May24 Q21"]}, "6.3": {"h": "<h2>Express<\/h2>\n<p><b>Express<\/b> is a minimal web framework for Node.js (<code>npm install express<\/code>). It adds <b>routing<\/b>, <b>middleware<\/b> and easy request/response helpers on top of the http module.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const express = require(&quot;express&quot;);\nconst app = express();\n\napp.use(express.json());                          // middleware: parse JSON bodies\napp.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));  // parse HTML form bodies\napp.use(express.static(&quot;public&quot;));                // serve files from /public\n\napp.get(&quot;/&quot;, (req, res) =&gt; res.sendFile(__dirname + &quot;/index.html&quot;));\napp.get(&quot;/hello/:name&quot;, (req, res) =&gt; res.send(&quot;Hello &quot; + req.params.name));   // route parameter\napp.get(&quot;/search&quot;, (req, res) =&gt; res.json({ q: req.query.q }));               // ?q=... query string\napp.post(&quot;/login&quot;, (req, res) =&gt; res.send(&quot;Welcome &quot; + req.body.username));   // form / JSON body\n\napp.listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;Server running on port 3000&quot;));<\/pre>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Where data comes from<\/th><th>Read with<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>URL path <code>/students/:id<\/code><\/td><td><code>req.params.id<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Query string <code>?page=2<\/code> (GET forms)<\/td><td><code>req.query.page<\/code><\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>Body (POST/PUT forms, JSON)<\/td><td><code>req.body<\/code> (needs urlencoded / json middleware)<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Responses: <code>res.send()<\/code>, <code>res.json()<\/code>, <code>res.status(404).json(…)<\/code>, <code>res.sendFile()<\/code>, <code>res.redirect(\"/x\")<\/code>. <b>Middleware<\/b> = a function <code>(req, res, next)<\/code> that runs before the route handler (logging, parsing, authentication) and calls <code>next()<\/code>.<\/p>\n<h2>REST APIs<\/h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Method<\/th><th>Route<\/th><th>Action<\/th><th>Success code<\/th><\/tr>\n<tr><td>GET<\/td><td><code>/api/students<\/code><\/td><td>list all<\/td><td>200<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>GET<\/td><td><code>/api/students/:id<\/code><\/td><td>one<\/td><td>200 (404 if missing)<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>POST<\/td><td><code>/api/students<\/code><\/td><td>create<\/td><td>201<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>PUT / PATCH<\/td><td><code>/api/students/:id<\/code><\/td><td>update<\/td><td>200<\/td><\/tr>\n<tr><td>DELETE<\/td><td><code>/api/students/:id<\/code><\/td><td>delete<\/td><td>200 / 204<\/td><\/tr><\/table>\n<p>Errors: 400 bad input, 404 not found, 409 conflict (duplicate), 500 server error. Test APIs with <b>Postman<\/b> (choose the method, URL, Body → raw → JSON) or <code>curl<\/code>.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q10", "Nov24 Q21", "Nxt25 Q23", "RJS Q34"]}, "6.4": {"h": "<h2>The full-stack pattern (the compulsory Q24)<\/h2>\n<p>Every \"Node + Express + MongoDB\" question has the same skeleton. Learn it once:<\/p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>Setup<\/b>: <code>npm init -y<\/code>, <code>npm install express mongoose<\/code>, start MongoDB.<\/li>\n<li><b>Imports and middleware<\/b>: <code>express()<\/code>, <code>express.json()<\/code> (APIs) and/or <code>express.urlencoded()<\/code> (HTML forms).<\/li>\n<li><b>Connect<\/b>: <code>mongoose.connect(\"mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/dbName\")<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><b>Schema and model<\/b> with the fields the question lists, plus <code>required<\/code> / <code>unique<\/code> / <code>min<\/code> / <code>max<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><b>Routes<\/b>, exactly as named in the question, each <code>async<\/code> with <code>try/catch<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li><b>Validation and errors<\/b>: 400 for bad input, 409 for duplicates (check with <code>findOne<\/code> first, and catch error 11000), 404 for not found, 500 otherwise.<\/li>\n<li><code>app.listen(port)<\/code>, then show how to test it (Postman or curl) with sample requests and responses.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"js\">const express = require(&quot;express&quot;);\nconst mongoose = require(&quot;mongoose&quot;);\nconst app = express();\napp.use(express.json());\n\nmongoose.connect(&quot;mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/libraryDB&quot;);\n\nconst Book = mongoose.model(&quot;Book&quot;, new mongoose.Schema({\n  title: { type: String, required: true, unique: true },\n  author: { type: String, required: true },\n  available: { type: Boolean, default: true }\n}));\n\napp.post(&quot;/api/books&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; {\n  try {\n    if (await Book.findOne({ title: req.body.title }))\n      return res.status(409).json({ message: &quot;Book already exists&quot; });\n    res.status(201).json(await Book.create(req.body));\n  } catch (err) {\n    res.status(err.name === &quot;ValidationError&quot; ? 400 : 500).json({ message: err.message });\n  }\n});\n\napp.get(&quot;/api/books&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; res.json(await Book.find()));\n\napp.put(&quot;/api/books/:title/issue&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; {\n  const b = await Book.findOneAndUpdate({ title: req.params.title }, { available: false }, { new: true });\n  b ? res.json(b) : res.status(404).json({ message: &quot;Not found&quot; });\n});\n\napp.delete(&quot;/api/books/:title&quot;, async (req, res) =&gt; {\n  const r = await Book.deleteOne({ title: req.params.title });\n  r.deletedCount ? res.json({ message: &quot;Deleted&quot; }) : res.status(404).json({ message: &quot;Not found&quot; });\n});\n\napp.listen(3000, () =&gt; console.log(&quot;Library API on port 3000&quot;));<\/pre>\n<p>This is the Library Book Management system from the Module 6 slides in compact form. The worked answers below (student records, user registration, course management) follow the same skeleton and were run against a real MongoDB, with the responses shown.<\/p>\n<p><b>Serving an HTML form instead of JSON<\/b> (Apr26 Q23 style): <code>app.get(\"/\")<\/code> sends the form with <code>res.sendFile<\/code>, the form posts to a route, <code>express.urlencoded()<\/code> fills <code>req.body<\/code>, the route saves it and replies with a message.<\/p>", "qs": ["Nov25 Q24", "Apr26 Q23", "RAS Q3"]}};
